desc:ZP Voiceover Unified Chain v4.1.5 - Voice Leveler - Paolo Balestri - BUS AUTO LIVE BROWNFIX3
options:gmem=ZPVoiceoverSharedBus
tags: voiceover voice leveler compressor limiter gate expander brown guard lufs rms paolo balestri zio paolo
//autror: Paolo Balestri - Zio Paolo
//variant: v4.1.5-circular-threshold-meters
// Contatto: social@paolobalestri.com
//
// CHANGELOG v4.1.5-circular-threshold-meters
// - Live circular detector rings: Gate, 1175, Major Tom and Limiter Ceiling.
// - Output: nascosto Output Auto Apply dalla barra host alta; il controllo resta nella GUI Output.
// - Output: AUTO calcola e applica live la correzione anche quando Capture e' pronta.
// - Capture resta memoria/display e non congela piu' out_trim_db.
// - BUS beta invariata.

// ============================================================================
// MANUALE UTENTE — Voiceover Unified Chain ZP v4.1.0-bus-tone-beta
// Plugin: Voiceover Unified Chain ZP | Autore: Paolo Balestri | Contatto: social@paolobalestri.com
// Sezione "living": si aggiorna ad ogni revisione DSP o UI significativa.
// ============================================================================
//
// ── PANORAMICA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Catena di elaborazione audio completa pensata per voiceover, podcast e
// doppiaggio. Integra in un unico plugin tutto il necessario: pulizia del
// segnale, compressione multistadio, limiting/clip controllato e controllo
// automatico del livello finale (Output).
//
// Ordine del segnale:
//   Input Trim → Input Smart Capture Gain → Gate/Expander → 1175 → LA2 → MajorTom
//   → Brown Guard → Voice Limiter/Clipper (zero latency + sat) → Output (manual gain + auto trim) → Final Safety Limiter
//
// ── INTERFACCIA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// GUI View  — pannelli grafici con knob, meter e pulsanti.
//             Attiva con il tasto GUI in testata.
// JSFX View — lista parametri host (OSARA, automazione, fine-tuning).
//             Attiva con il tasto JSFX in testata.
//
// La finestra ha larghezza fissa 792 px. Se la cornice è più stretta,
// il contenuto scorre orizzontalmente con il trackpad (two-finger swipe).
// La scrollbar orizzontale appare in fondo quando la finestra è stretta.
// Il contenuto verticale scorre con la rotella del mouse nell'area pannelli.
//
// ── TESTATA (sempre visibile) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Riga Preset    NAT BRD DNS WRM MCH FLT
//   Carica uno dei 6 profili predefiniti (vedi sezione Profili sotto).
//   Il profilo attivo si illumina in verde. Se modifichi manualmente un
//   parametro dopo aver caricato un profilo, la luce resta ma i valori
//   divergono — è il comportamento atteso (non c'è tracking automatico).
//
// Riga ON/OFF    IN EXP 1175 LA2 MT BRN LIM OUT
//   Attiva/disattiva ogni modulo individualmente. Spento = grigio, acceso
//   = colore del modulo. OUT controlla il modulo Output.
//
// Riga View      1-IN 2-EXP 3-1175 4-LA2 5-MT 6-BRN 7-LIM 8-OUT
//   Mostra o nasconde il pannello grafico di ogni modulo nell'area di
//   contenuto. Nascondere un pannello NON spegne il modulo.
//
// Riga Nav       DBG | GUI | JSFX
//   DBG mostra informazioni diagnostiche.
//   GUI / JSFX commuta la vista principale.
//
// Spia S/M:
//   Indicatore automatico del formato canale host: S = stereo, M = mono.
//   Non e' un pulsante: segue il numero canali comunicato da REAPER.
//   In mono applica la compensazione +3 dB ai meter LUFS e al target LUFS
//   dell'Output Auto Trim, cosi' lettura e inseguimento lavorano sulla
//   stessa scala percettiva.
//
// Indicatori stato moduli (sotto il titolo, a sinistra):
//   Pallini colorati IN · EXP · 1175 · LA2 · MT · LIM che si accendono
//   col colore del modulo quando il modulo è attivo.
//
// Preset corrente: riga verde sotto i pallini (es. "Preset: Natural").
// I preset non modificano Input Smart/Capture: una calibrazione gia' fatta
// resta attiva e salvata anche cambiando profilo della catena.
//
// ── MODULI — DESCRIZIONE E CONTROLLI ────────────────────────────────────────
//
// 1 · INPUT SMART
//   Doppio stadio: InTrim (gain manuale fisso) + Smart Capture Gain.
//   Prima di avviare CAP il primo knob del pannello e' GainIn: gain staging
//   manuale in dBFS tramite InTrim. Quando CAP e' in corso o LOCK, lo stesso
//   spazio diventa Target e governa il target RMS della cattura Smart.
//   - Target  [-30 .. -8 dB RMS]  Livello RMS obiettivo della cattura.
//   - MAX     [0 .. 12 dB]        Correzione massima applicabile (±MAX).
//   - Speed   [0.2 .. 8 s]        Rampa del trim dopo la cattura.
//   MAX e Speed restano grigi finche' CAP non e' in corso o LOCK.
//   La cattura e' manuale: premi CAP/NEW nel box Smart, poi il plugin misura
//   il tempo scelto dal piccolo knob azzurro interno (20-90 s), calcola il trim
//   necessario e lo blocca. Il valore catturato e il tempo scelto sono salvati
//   con il progetto e ricaricati senza dover ricatturare.
//
// 2 · EXPANDER (Gate)
//   Espansore downward ispirato al Tukan DL24. Attenua il segnale sotto
//   la soglia — utile per ridurre fondo ambiente, respiri e rumori di stanza.
//   - THRS    [-70 .. -10 dB]     Soglia di apertura.
//   - RANGE   [-40 .. 0 dB]       Attenuazione massima quando chiuso.
//   - HYST    [-12 .. 0 dB]       Isteresi: la soglia di chiusura è THRS+HYST
//                                  (evita pompaggio su segnali al limite).
//   - ATTK    [0.1 .. 30 ms]      Tempo di apertura.
//   - REL     [20 .. 2000 ms]     Tempo di chiusura.
//   - HPF     [Off .. 10 kHz]     Filtro passa-alto sul sidechain
//                                  (dorato SC, non filtra l audio)
//   - Curve   [0 .. 48 dB]         Knee/morbidezza dell expander:
//                                  piu alto = transizione piu dolce.
//                                  (elimina i bassi dall'analisi: rumori
//                                  di struttura, AC, ecc.).
//   Meter: IN · GR (riduzione) · OUT
//
// 3 · 1175  (compressore FET)
//   Compressore a detection RMS con release opzionalmente lineare (profilo
//   Dense). Simula il comportamento aggressivo di un 1176.
//   - THRS    [-60 .. 0 dB]       Soglia.
//   - RATIO   [1 .. 20]           Rapporto di compressione.
//   - MKP     [-12 .. +18 dB]     Makeup gain post-compressione.
//   - ATTK    [20 .. 2000 µs]     Attacco (microsecondi).
//   - REL     [20 .. 1000 ms]     Release.
//   - MIX     [0 .. 100 %]        Parallel compression (dry/wet).
//   - SC      [Off .. 10 kHz]      HPF sidechain dorato: evita che basse/plosive
//                                  guidino la compressione; fino a zona de-esser.
//   Meter: IN · GR · OUT
//
// 4 · LA2  (compressore ottico)
//   Simula un LA-2A: attack e release fissi, controllo con Peak Reduction.
//   - P-Red   [0 .. 100]          Riduzione del picco (più alto = più compressione).
//   - GAIN    [-12 .. +18 dB]     Makeup gain.
//   - MIX     [0 .. 100 %]        Parallel compression.
//   - COMP/LIM                    Modalità COMP (ratio 3:1) o LIM (ratio 10:1).
//   Attack ≈ 10 ms, Release ≈ 500 ms (fissi, come l'originale).
//   - SC      [Off .. 10 kHz]      HPF sidechain dorato sulla detection LA2.
//   Meter: IN · GR · OUT
//
// 5 · MAJOR TOM  (compressore VCA)
//   Compressore versatile con detection configurabile e auto makeup.
//   - THRS    [-60 .. 0 dB]       Soglia.
//   - RATIO   [1 .. 20]           Rapporto di compressione.
//   - MKP     [-12 .. +12 dB]     Makeup manuale (usato se Auto Makeup = No).
//   - MIX     [0 .. 100 %]        Parallel compression.
//   - ATTK    [0.2 .. 50 ms]      Scala l'attacco program-dependent.
//                                  10 ms = comportamento originale.
//   - Hard/Soft                   Knee duro o morbido (onset graduale).
//   - Peak/RMS                    Detection su picco o RMS.
//   - FFW/FFB                     Feedforward (analisi pre) o Feedback (post).
//   - NoAM/AMU                    No auto makeup / Auto makeup attivo.
//   Attack e release sono adattativi (si adattano automaticamente al livello
//   di overdrive — più il segnale supera la soglia, più l'attacco è rapido).
//   Meter: IN · GR · OUT
//
// 6 · BROWN GUARD  (correzione tonale dinamica)
//   Guardiano tonale a 4 bande: legge lo sbilanciamento rispetto alla curva
//   brown scelta e corregge in modo dinamico. Puo' contenere zone dure o
//   gonfie senza usare un EQ statico.
//   - Slope   [-3 .. +8 dB/oct]   Inclinazione target della curva.
//   - Amt     [0 .. 150 %]        Quantita' di correzione.
//   - Atk     [20 .. 2000 ms]     Reazione quando deve correggere.
//   - Rel     [100 .. 6000 ms]    Ritorno verso neutro.
//   - STD/BAL/DRK/BRT             Preset interni Brown, ora toggle:
//                                  clic sul preset acceso = torna Manual Flat.
//   - Punti Slope Map             Drag verticale sui quattro punti:
//                                  trim manuale ±6 dB su campane larghe.
//                                  Drag laterale su tutti e quattro:
//                                  sposta la frequenza focus senza fare shelf.
//   - AMU                         Auto make-up post-Brown: compensa lentamente
//                                  la perdita di livello percepita, max +6 dB.
//                                  E' OFF di default.
//   Meter: IN · TONE · OUT
//
// 7 · VOICE LIMITER / CLIPPER  (zero latency + saturazione opzionale)
//   Controllo picchi e densita' pensato per voce parlata, non per mastering.
//   - Ceil    [-9 .. -0.1 dBFS]   Soffitto di uscita.
//   - Soft    [0 .. 20 ms]         Ammorbidisce la presa; 0 = massima fermezza.
//   - Rel     [5 .. 500 ms]       Release.
//   - PreG    [-12 .. +12 dB]     Pre-gain prima del limiter.
//   - SAT     [0 .. 100 %]        Saturazione armonica via tanh (aggiunge calore).
//   Display SAT: finestra grafica a destra dei knob che mostra la curva di
//   trasferimento della saturazione in tempo reale.
//   Non usa lookahead ne' PDC: resta stabile nel monitoring REAPER e non introduce
//   ritardi variabili. Per protezione finale di consegna usa il Final Limiter OUT.
//   Nota di taratura: il display Ceil mostra +0.7 dB rispetto al valore DSP
//   per compensare lo sforamento tipico del blocco limiter. E' intenzionale:
//   impostare -0.7 nel controllo produce lettura 0.0 nel display.
//   Meter: IN · GR · OUT
//
// ── OUTPUT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Il modulo Output è un controller di livello finale con limiter di sicurezza in coda. Si trova in fondo alla
// finestra ed è sempre visibile (o attivabile via pulsante OUT in testata).
//
// ZONA TARGET (sinistra):
//   Preset output — POD / AUD / MIX / BRD / RAD
//     Caricano configurazioni di target predefinite per piattaforme:
//     POD=Podcast, AUD=Audiolibro, MIX=Voiceover su musica, BRD=Broadcast,
//     RAD=Radio/Spot.
//
//   - Gain    [-12 .. +12 dB]       Makeup finale Output, dopo tutta la catena.
//   - MaxTrm  [0 .. 18 dB]          Correzione automatica massima consentita.
//   I knob sopra (riga 1) sono attivi solo con OUT acceso e non cambiano
//   l'azione dei compressori; GainIn resta nel modulo Input.
//
//   - LUFS    [-23 .. -9 dB LUFS]   Target LUFS, attivo solo in modo LUFS.
//   - RMS     [-30 .. -9 dB]        Target RMS, attivo solo in modo RMS.
//   - L+R     [-29 .. -9 dB]        Target unico combinato, attivo solo in L+R.
//   - Speed   [0.1 .. 5 s]          Velocita' dell'auto trim.
//   I target della riga 2 sono esclusivi: LUFS accende solo LUFS, RMS accende
//   solo RMS, L+R accende un target unico. I knob non attivi restano grigi.
//   - Auto Target [Off/LUFS/RMS/L+R] Modalita' dell'auto trim:
//       Off  = solo Gain finale Output, nessun inseguimento automatico.
//              Il Final Safety Limiter resta bypassato finche' non lo accendi.
//       LUFS = corregge lentamente verso il solo target LUFS.
//       RMS  = corregge verso il solo target RMS.
//       L+R  = target unico: LUFS = L+R +1 dB, RMS = L+R -1 dB.
//
//   In L+R non puoi incrociare LUFS alto e RMS basso: un solo knob governa
//   entrambi con rapporto fisso, cosi' la GUI racconta il comportamento reale.
//
// ZONA LIVE (destra):
//   Meter verticali seghettati M · S · I · RMS · TP
//     M  = LUFS Momentanei  (costante 400 ms)
//     S  = LUFS Short-term  (costante 3 s)
//     I  = LUFS Integrati   (cumulativo da Play, reference per il mastering)
//     LRA= Loudness Range   (differenza percentile 10°-95° — dinamica del programma)
//     RMS= livello RMS post-Output
//     TP = true peak stimato post-plugin
//
//   Box Misure (a destra dei meter):
//     Mostra i valori numerici. Si CONGELA allo stop del trasporto così puoi
//     leggere le misure finali senza che il display si azzeri. Si resetta
//     automaticamente al prossimo play.
//     TP = true peak stimato post-plugin con interpolazione 4x, mostrato
//     con hold stile meter esterno per essere leggibile. "max" resta il massimo
//     reale da Play corrente.
//
// ── PROFILI PREDEFINITI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   NAT — Natural VO
//     Compressione equilibrata per voce naturale e podcast.
//     Expander morbido con Curve/knee, 1175 con ratio 4:1, makeup moderato, limiter -1 dBFS.
//
//   BRD — Broadcast Tight
//     Compressione più aggressiva per standard broadcast (EBU R128).
//     Gate leggermente più chiuso, 1175 con ratio 6:1, LA2 più attivo.
//
//   DNS — Dense Promo
//     Profilo promotivo/promo ad alta densità. Attiva un soft-clipper
//     tanh prima del limiter (stage interno dense_mode). Compressioni
//     parallele 1175 + LA2 + MT in mix parziale. Target LUFS -15.
//
//   WRM — Warm Narration
//     Ratio bassi (2.8:1 sul 1175, 2:1 su MajorTom), release lunghi,
//     mix parallelo 70-80%. Suono aperto e naturale per audiolibri.
//
//   MCH — Match Chain Base
//     Profilo calibrato su -18 LUFS / -3 dBFS come punto di partenza
//     per bilanciamento con tracce pre-masterate. Valori ottimizzati
//     manualmente in sessione.
//
//   FLT — Flat Start
//     Tutti i moduli disattivati, gain neutro. Punto di partenza per
//     costruire una chain da zero senza preset.
//
// ── WORKFLOW CONSIGLIATO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. Carica un profilo (NAT per iniziare).
// 2. Ascolta la voce: regola Gate THRS e RANGE finché i rumori di stanza
//    spariscono senza tagliare le consonanti.
// 3. 1175: abbassa THRS finché il GR meter mostra -4/-8 dB sui picchi.
//    Aggiusta RATIO e MKP per recuperare il livello.
// 4. LA2: usa P-Red per aggiungere "corpo" e glue. Aggiusta GAIN.
// 5. MajorTom: compressione lenta e musicale. Prova FFB + Soft per
//    suoni più trasparenti. Attiva Auto Makeup.
// 6. Voice Limiter: Ceil a -1.0 dBFS come standard. Soft basso per voce ferma;
//    SAT al 5-15% per calore senza distorsione udibile.
// 7. Output: scegli un preset output (POD o AUD), attiva Auto L+R e
//    lascia che il plugin insegua il target LUFS nelle sessioni lunghe.
//    Per mix su musica: usa Auto L+R e regola il target unico L+R.
//
// ── TASTI E SHORTCUT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Knob:
//   Drag verticale     — regolazione normale
//   SHIFT + drag       — precisione fine (movimento ridotto ~10x)
//   Doppio click       — reset al valore default del knob
//
// Pulsante RST (Output):
//   Click singolo      — azzera tutti i parametri Output ai default
//                        e deseleziona il preset attivo
//   NON richiede doppio click (diversamente dai knob)
//
// ── NOTE TECNICHE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// - @slider: gestisce solo profili e visibilità host list.
// - @sample: tutto il DSP + telemetria per la GUI (ui_*_in/act/out_db).
// - @gfx: render puro. Tutte le coordinate usano PX=10-scroll_x, PW=770
//   come costanti — layout fisso indipendente da gfx_w.
// - @gfx non scrive variabili DSP: quando REAPER e' fermo puo' esserci audio
//   live in monitoring, quindi i reset di gain/stato devono restare in @sample.
// - La finestra può essere ridimensionata ma il layout NON si adatta:
//   sotto 792 px la scrollbar orizzontale permette di accedere a tutto.
// - v4.0.31: primo passaggio leggibilita' UI, canvas 720x1180,
//   pannelli modulo piu' alti/largi e font base knob/meter uniformati.
// - v4.0.32: il display Curve dell'Expander mostra anche il punto HYST
//   (soglia di chiusura THRS+HYST) con marker dedicato.
// - v4.0.33: CAP Input Smart riproporzionato e barra tips inferiore
//   ampliata su due righe per migliore leggibilita'.
// - v4.0.34: testata e pulsantiera ingrandite, font pulsanti modulo
//   uniformati al riferimento Brown Guard, tips su due righe omogenee.
// - v4.0.35: valori CapSec e label SC ingranditi e distanziati
//   dal knob per migliorare la lettura.
// - v4.0.36: overlay tips a messaggio unico con wrap automatico
//   su due righe quando il testo e' troppo lungo per la finestra.
// - v4.0.37: testata piu' leggibile, font descrittivi +2 pt e
//   grigi critici sostituiti dall'azzurrino della riga versione.
// - v4.0.38: Output readability pass, Auto dB/Capture/Measure
//   armonizzati con font piu' leggibili e meno grigio su grigio.
// - v4.0.39: Output Auto Trim, Auto dB e Capture marcati con
//   fondo dorato leggero per evidenziare la funzione comune.
// - v4.0.40: pannello Output riordinato in flusso logico:
//   Target -> Auto dB/Capture -> Measure -> LIVE meter.
// - v4.0.41: Measure Output allargato e spia play spostata per
//   lasciare leggibile la riga descrittiva del box.
// - v4.0.42: LRA allineato al criterio ZP Meter v43: short-term
//   gated con soglia relativa energia media -20 LU.
// - v4.0.43: scale GUI Expander allineate agli slider reali:
//   THRS -70/-10, RANGE -40/0, HYST -12/0.
// - v4.0.44: richiamo profili/Brown reso sicuro al caricamento progetto:
//   i preset si applicano solo da azione esplicita, non durante il load.
// - v4.0.45: variante non distruttiva con Brown Guard AMU interno:
//   pulsante ON/OFF nel pannello Brown e compensazione lenta post-Brown.
//   I preset Brown sono toggle; spenti tornano a Manual Flat e lasciano
//   lo Slope come controllo principale.
//   I punti della Slope Map sono focus manuali a campana larga salvati col
//   progetto; tutti hanno drag laterale, inclusi LOW/HIGH, senza HPF/LPF.
// - v4.0.46: release stabile della linea Brown Focus; overlay pulsanti
//   e manuale allineati alle funzioni definitive.
// - v4.0.47: TP max spostato nel thread audio: il massimo non dipende piu'
//   dal refresh della GUI e intercetta anche picchi molto brevi.
// - v4.0.48: separati TP corrente/barra, TP leggibile e TP max: la barra
//   LIVE segue il segnale senza il doppio hold del numero.
// - v4.0.49: Major Tom aggiunge ATTK interno 0.2-50 ms. Default 10 ms:
//   conserva il comportamento precedente ma rende scalabile la presa.
// - v4.0.50-ui-safe-dev: copia non distruttiva. Preset globali spostati
//   lontano dagli ON/OFF moduli; Output piu' leggibile con font knob
//   maggiorati e bande GAIN/REG. Nessuna modifica al DSP.
// - v4.0.51-scale-brown-dev: nuova copia. GUI allargata circa 10%,
//   preset testata avvicinati alla label senza testo Match ridondante,
//   Brown Guard piu' alto con Slope Map grande e lettura frequenze.
// - v4.0.52-output-gain-bypass-dev: nuova copia. Output Gain separato
//   da Input Gain, controlli Output inattivi a modulo spento, meter moduli
//   spenti in BYP e Dense legato al Limiter.
// - v4.0.53-ui-spacing-dev: nuova copia. Brown Slope Map piu' larga con
//   focus colore sui punti attivi; Output Auto dB/Capture e Target con
//   font e spaziature piu' uniformi.
// - v4.0.54-knob-labels-dev: nuova copia. Etichette knob uniformate
//   in maiuscolo e dimensione coerente con 1175.
// - v4.0.55-brown-amount-dev: nuova copia. I punti della Brown Slope Map
//   scalano col controllo AMT e non restano piu' un EQ statico a gain pieno.
// - v4.0.56-brown-din-dev: nuova copia. Aggiunto bottone DIN nel Brown
//   Guard: OFF = punti EQ fissi, ON = punti scalati da AMT.
// - v4.1.0-bus-tone-beta: copia beta BUS. Aggiunto Bus Tone post-Brown
//   con punti voce fissi + air guard dinamico e Voice Bus Limiter con
//   detector HPF, Max GR interno e release program-dependent.
// - WRM aggiornato come preset personale Paolo dal setup Brown AMU del
//   2026-05-01, con Brown BRT+AMU e Slope Map manuale.
// - Input Smart manuale: prima di CAP il primo knob e' GainIn/InTrim;
//   Target/MAX/Speed diventano operativi solo con CAP in corso o LOCK.
// - I profili vengono applicati solo al cambio profilo, non ad ogni
//   @slider, per non sovrascrivere modifiche manuali successive.
// - Accessibility mode bloccata ON internamente (OSARA).
// - Frequenze operative: il plugin elabora ad ogni campione audio (srate-agnostico:
//   funziona a 44.1 / 48 / 88.2 / 96 kHz senza modifiche). I coefficienti DSP
//   vengono ricalcolati automaticamente al cambio sessione.
//   Meter: logica derivata da ZP Loudness Meter v43, con finestre reali
//   400 ms / 3 s, LUFS-I con gate relativo e LRA da short-term gated.
//   Auto S/M: get_host_numchan() in @gfx, fallback num_ch; la compensazione
//   mono +3 dB entra sia nei meter LUFS sia nell'Output Auto Target LUFS.
//   LRA: campionato a 10 Hz con algoritmo EBU R128 (istogramma P95-P10 + gate -20LU).
// ============================================================================

in_pin:Input L
in_pin:Input R
out_pin:Output L
out_pin:Output R

slider1:profile=5<0,6,1{Manual,Natural VO,Broadcast Tight,Dense Promo,Warm Narration,Match Chain Base (-18/-3),Flat Start (All Zero)}>Profile

slider2:in_smart_on=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Input Smart Gain
slider50:in_trim=0<-18,18,0.1>Input Trim [dB]
slider3:in_smart_target=-18<-30,-8,0.1>Input Smart Target RMS [dB]
slider4:in_smart_max=6<0,12,0.1>Input Smart Max Trim [dB]
slider5:in_smart_speed=2.0<0.2,8,0.1>Input Smart Speed [s]

slider6:gate_on=1<0,1,1{Bypass,On}>1 Gate On
slider7:gate_thresh=-46<-70,-10,0.1>1 Gate Threshold [dB]
slider8:gate_range=-8<-40,0,0.1>1 Gate Range [dB]
slider9:gate_hyst=-3<-12,0,0.1>1 Gate Hysteresis [dB]
slider10:gate_att=2<0.1,30,0.1>1 Gate Attack [ms]
slider11:gate_rel=180<20,2000,1>1 Gate Release [ms]
slider12:gate_hpf=80<0,10000,1>1 Expander SC HPF [Hz] (0=Off)

slider13:c1175_on=1<0,1,1{Bypass,On}>2 1175 On
slider14:c1175_thresh=-24<-60,0,0.1>2 1175 Threshold [dB]
slider15:c1175_ratio=4<1,20,0.1>2 1175 Ratio
slider16:c1175_makeup=4<-12,18,0.1>2 1175 Makeup [dB]
slider17:c1175_att_us=200<20,2000,10>2 1175 Attack [us]
slider18:c1175_rel=60<20,1000,1>2 1175 Release [ms]
slider19:c1175_mix=100<0,100,0.1>2 1175 Mix [%]

slider20:la2_on=1<0,1,1{Bypass,On}>3 LA2 On
slider21:la2_peakred=38<0,100,0.1>3 LA2 Peak Reduction
slider22:la2_mode=0<0,1,1{Compress,Limit}>3 LA2 Ratio Mode
slider23:la2_gain=3<-12,18,0.1>3 LA2 Gain [dB]
slider24:la2_mix=100<0,100,0.1>3 LA2 Mix [%]

slider25:mt_on=1<0,1,1{Bypass,On}>4 MajorTom On
slider26:mt_thresh=-14<-60,0,0.1>4 MajorTom Threshold [dB]
slider27:mt_ratio=2.6<1,20,0.1>4 MajorTom Ratio
slider28:mt_knee=1<0,1,1{Hard,Soft}>4 MajorTom Knee
slider29:mt_detect=1<0,1,1{Peak,RMS}>4 MajorTom Detection
slider30:mt_source=0<0,1,1{Feedforward,Feedback}>4 MajorTom Source
slider31:mt_automu=1<0,1,1{No,Yes}>4 MajorTom Auto Makeup
slider32:mt_makeup=0<-12,12,0.1>4 MajorTom Makeup [dB]
slider33:mt_mix=100<0,100,0.1>4 MajorTom Mix [%]

slider34:lim_on=1<0,1,1{Bypass,On}>5 Limiter On
slider35:lim_ceiling=-1<-9,-0.1,0.1>5 Limiter Ceiling [dB]
slider36:lim_look=0<0,20,0.1>5 Limiter Soft [ms]
slider37:lim_rel=90<5,500,1>5 Limiter Release [ms]
slider38:lim_pregain=0<-12,12,0.1>5 Limiter Pre-Gain [dB]
slider39:lim_sat=0<0,100,0.1>5 Limiter Saturation [%]

slider57:brn_on=0<0,1,1{Bypass,On}>6 Brown Guard On
slider58:brn_preset=0<0,4,1{Manual,STD Flat,VO Balance,Darker,Brighter}>6 Brown Preset
slider59:brn_in_trim=0<-24,24,0.1>6 Brown Input Trim [dB]
slider60:brn_slope=1.0<-3,8,0.1>6 Brown Target Slope [dB/oct]
slider61:brn_amount=60<0,150,1>6 Brown Amount [%]
slider62:brn_attack=200<20,2000,1>6 Brown Attack [ms]
slider63:brn_release=1400<100,6000,10>6 Brown Release [ms]

slider40:out_mode=0<0,3,1{Off,LUFS,RMS,L+R}>Out Auto Target Mode
slider41:out_target_lufs=-16<-30,-10,0.1>Out Target LUFS [dB]
slider42:out_target_rms=-18<-30,-8,0.1>Out Target RMS [dB]
slider43:out_trim_max=6<0,18,0.1>Out Max Auto Trim [dB]
slider44:out_speed=1.2<0.1,5,0.1>Out Auto Trim Speed [s]
slider45:out_makeup=0<-12,12,0.1>Out Manual Makeup [dB]
slider46:c1175_sc_hpf=0<0,10000,1>2 1175 SC HPF [Hz] (0=Off)
slider47:compact_page=0<0,8,1{Quick,Input,Gate,1175,LA2,MajorTom,Brown,Limiter,Output}>JSFX Page
slider48:la2_sc_hpf=0<0,10000,1>3 LA2 SC HPF [Hz] (0=Off)
slider49:gate_curve=24<0,48,0.1>1 Expander Curve Knee [dB]
slider51:mt_sc_hpf=0<0,10000,1>4 MajorTom SC HPF [Hz] (0=Off)
slider52:gfx_view=0<0,1,1{GUI View,JSFX View}>GFX View
slider53:ui_block_mask=255<0,255,1>GUI Block Mask
slider54:out_final_lim_on=0<0,1,1{Off,On}>Final Limiter On
slider55:out_target_lr=-17<-29,-9,0.1>Out Target L+R [dB]
slider64:capture_seconds=30<20,90,1>-Legacy Capture Time (unused)
slider56:out_enable=1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Out Module Enable
slider65:out_in_gain=0<-12,12,0.1>-Out Input Gain [dB]
slider66:out_auto_apply=0<0,1,1{MAN,AUTO}>-Output Auto Apply

@init
// ZP Shared Bus: stato osservativo, nessuna modifica al percorso audio.
ZP_BUS_MAGIC = 905026;
ZP_BUS_VERSION = 220;
ZP_BUS_ID = 10;
ZP_BUS_FRESH_SEC = 2;
function zp_bus_boot() (
  gmem[0] != ZP_BUS_MAGIC || gmem[1] < ZP_BUS_VERSION ? (
    gmem[0] = ZP_BUS_MAGIC;
    gmem[1] = ZP_BUS_VERSION;
    gmem[2] = 1;
    gmem[3] = 0;
    gmem[4] = 0;
    gmem[10]=gmem[11]=gmem[12]=gmem[20]=gmem[21]=gmem[22]=0;
    gmem[30]=gmem[31]=gmem[32]=gmem[40]=gmem[41]=gmem[42]=0;
    gmem[50]=gmem[51]=gmem[52]=gmem[60]=gmem[61]=gmem[62]=0;
  );
);
function zp_bus_read() local(now) (
  zp_bus_boot();
  now=time_precise(); zp_bus_now=now;
  zp_bus_profile = max(1, min(6, floor(gmem[2] + 0.5)));
  zp_bus_master_conn=gmem[40]==905040 ? (now-gmem[41]<=ZP_BUS_FRESH_SEC?2:1) : 0;
  zp_bus_probe_conn=gmem[50]==905050 ? (now-gmem[51]<=ZP_BUS_FRESH_SEC?2:1) : 0;
  zp_bus_master_ok=zp_bus_master_conn>0; zp_bus_probe_ok=zp_bus_probe_conn>0;
);
function zp_bus_refresh(plugin_id) (
  zp_bus_boot(); gmem[plugin_id]=905000+plugin_id; gmem[plugin_id+1]=time_precise(); gmem[plugin_id+2]+=1; zp_bus_read();
);
zp_bus_refresh(ZP_BUS_ID);
ext_tail_size = -1;
ext_noinit = 1;
last_profile = -100;
ui_scroll_y = 0;
ui_max_scroll = 0;
last_mouse_wheel = 0;
ui_scroll_dragging = 0;
ui_scroll_drag_start_y = 0;
ui_scroll_drag_start_scroll = 0;
ui_prev_mouse_down = 0;
ui_hover_id = 0;
ui_content_pass = 0;
ui_host_visibility_state = -1;
ui_host_page_state = -1;
last_knob_click_slider = -1;
last_knob_click_time = 0;
mouse_state = 0;
drag_id = -1;
drag_start_y = 0;
drag_start_val = 0;
gfx_view = 0;
compact_page = 0;
auto_mono_mode = num_ch < 2 ? 1 : 0;
auto_mono_host_ch = num_ch;
auto_mono_from_gfx = 0;
in_capture_seconds <= 0 ? in_capture_seconds = 30;
out_capture_seconds <= 0 ? out_capture_seconds = 30;

function db2gain(x) (10^(x*0.05));
function gain2db(x) (20*log(max(x,0.000000000001))/log(10));
function clamp(x,lo,hi) (x < lo ? lo : (x > hi ? hi : x));
function slider_mask(sl_id) ( 2 ^ (sl_id - 1); );
function mono_lufs_comp() ( auto_mono_mode >= 0.5 ? 3.0 : 0.0; );
function out_lr_lufs_target() ( clamp(out_target_lr + 1, -30, -10); );
function out_lr_rms_target() ( clamp(out_target_lr - 1, -30, -8); );
function zap_denorm(x) ( abs(x) < 0.00000000000000000001 ? 0 : x; );
function refresh_in_smart_capture_trim()
(
  in_smart_capture_ready >= 0.5 ? (
    in_smart_capture_trim_db = clamp(in_smart_target - in_smart_capture_rms_db, -in_smart_max, in_smart_max);
  );
);
function reset_in_smart_capture()
(
  in_smart_capture_sum = 0;
  in_smart_capture_count = 0;
  in_smart_capture_progress = 0;
  in_smart_capture_ready = 0;
  in_smart_capture_state = 1;
  in_smart_capture_rms_db = -100;
  in_smart_capture_trim_db = 0;
);
function commit_in_smart_capture()
local(avg_pow)
(
  in_smart_capture_count > 0 ? (
    avg_pow = in_smart_capture_sum / max(1, in_smart_capture_count);
    in_smart_capture_rms_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(avg_pow, 0.000000000001)));
    in_smart_capture_ready = 1;
    in_smart_capture_state = 2;
    in_smart_capture_progress = 100;
    refresh_in_smart_capture_trim();
  );
);

// Output Smart Capture: clone indipendente dell'Input Smart Capture, con tempo proprio.
function out_capture_target_db() local(m, lufs_tgt) (
  m = clamp(floor(out_mode + 0.5), 0, 3);
  lufs_tgt = out_target_lufs - mono_lufs_comp();
  m == 2 ? out_target_rms :
  m == 3 ? (((out_lr_lufs_target() - mono_lufs_comp()) + out_lr_rms_target()) * 0.5) :
  lufs_tgt;
);
function refresh_out_smart_capture_trim() (
  out_smart_capture_ready >= 0.5 ? (
    out_smart_capture_trim_db = clamp(out_capture_target_db() - out_smart_capture_rms_db, -out_trim_cap, out_trim_cap);
  );
);
function reset_out_smart_capture() (
  out_smart_capture_sum = 0; out_smart_capture_count = 0; out_smart_capture_progress = 0;
  out_smart_capture_ready = 0; out_smart_capture_state = 0; out_smart_capture_rms_db = -100;
  out_smart_capture_trim_db = 0; out_smart_capture_smooth_trim = 0;
);
function prime_out_smart_capture() (
  out_smart_capture_sum = 0; out_smart_capture_count = 0; out_smart_capture_progress = 0;
  out_smart_capture_ready = 0; out_smart_capture_state = 1; out_smart_capture_rms_db = -100;
  out_smart_capture_trim_db = 0; out_smart_capture_smooth_trim = 0;
);
function commit_out_smart_capture() local(avg_pow) (
  out_smart_capture_count > 0 ? (
    avg_pow = out_smart_capture_sum / max(1, out_smart_capture_count);
    out_smart_capture_rms_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(avg_pow, 0.000000000001)));
    out_smart_capture_ready = 1; out_smart_capture_state = 2; out_smart_capture_progress = 100;
    refresh_out_smart_capture_trim();
  );
);
function brn_onepole_coef(freq) local(f) ( f = clamp(freq, 5, srate * 0.45); 1 - exp(-2*$pi*f/srate); );
function brn_oct_from_1k(freq) ( log(max(freq,1) / 1000) / log(2); );
// Usata da @slider durante reset/preset Brown: deve essere definita prima
// della sezione @slider, non soltanto tra gli helper grafici di @gfx.
function brn_reset_xmove_for_freq(freq, base, scale)
(
  clamp(log(max(freq,1) / max(base,1)) / log(2) / max(0.0001, scale), -8, 8);
);
function show_slider_range(lo, hi)
local(j)
(
  j = lo;
  loop(hi - lo + 1,
    slider_show(slider_mask(j), 1);
    j += 1;
  );
);

function apply_host_slider_visibility(show_host)
local(i, page)
(
  // Stable path used in Stagekeeper: per-slider bitmask.
  page = clamp(floor(compact_page + 0.5), 0, 8);
  ui_host_visibility_state != show_host || ui_host_page_state != page ? (
    i = 1;
    loop(64,
      slider_show(slider_mask(i), 0);
      i += 1;
    );
    slider_show(slider65, 0);
    slider_show(slider66, 0);

    show_host ? (
      page == 0 ? (
        slider_show(slider_mask(1), 1);  // Profile
        slider_show(slider_mask(2), 1);  // Input Smart Gain
        slider_show(slider_mask(6), 1);  // Gate On
        slider_show(slider_mask(13), 1); // 1175 On
        slider_show(slider_mask(20), 1); // LA2 On
        slider_show(slider_mask(25), 1); // MajorTom On
        slider_show(slider_mask(46), 1); // 1175 SC HPF
        slider_show(slider_mask(48), 1); // LA2 SC HPF
        slider_show(slider_mask(51), 1); // MajorTom SC HPF
        slider_show(slider_mask(57), 1); // Brown Guard On
        slider_show(slider_mask(34), 1); // Limiter On
        slider_show(slider_mask(56), 1); // Output On
      ) :
      page == 1 ? ( show_slider_range(2, 5); show_slider_range(50, 50); ) :
      page == 2 ? ( show_slider_range(6, 12); slider_show(slider_mask(49), 1); ) :
      page == 3 ? ( show_slider_range(13, 19); slider_show(slider_mask(46), 1); ) :
      page == 4 ? ( show_slider_range(20, 24); slider_show(slider_mask(48), 1); ) :
      page == 5 ? ( show_slider_range(25, 33); slider_show(slider_mask(51), 1); ) :
      page == 6 ? show_slider_range(57, 63) :
      page == 7 ? show_slider_range(34, 39) :
      page == 8 ? ( show_slider_range(40, 45); show_slider_range(50, 50); show_slider_range(54, 56); );

      // Keep navigation first in OSARA/host lists.
      slider_show(slider_mask(47), 1);
      slider_show(slider_mask(52), 1);

      // Other internal controls stay controlled by the mini GUI.
      slider_show(slider_mask(53), 0);
    );

    ui_host_visibility_state = show_host;
    ui_host_page_state = page;
  );
);

function tanh_fast(x)
(
  x > 3 ? 0.995 :
  x < -3 ? -0.995 :
  x*(27 + x*x)/(27 + 9*x*x);
);

function biquad_set_hp(fc, q)
instance(a0,a1,a2,b1,b2)
local(w0, c, s, alpha, b0n,b1n,b2n,a0n,a1n,a2n)
(
  w0 = 2*$pi*fc/srate;
  c = cos(w0);
  s = sin(w0);
  alpha = s/(2*q);

  b0n = (1 + c)*0.5;
  b1n = -(1 + c);
  b2n = (1 + c)*0.5;
  a0n = 1 + alpha;
  a1n = -2*c;
  a2n = 1 - alpha;

  a0 = b0n/a0n;
  a1 = b1n/a0n;
  a2 = b2n/a0n;
  b1 = a1n/a0n;
  b2 = a2n/a0n;
);

function biquad_set_hs(fc, q, dbgain)
instance(a0,a1,a2,b1,b2)
local(A,w0,c,s,alpha,beta,b0n,b1n,b2n,a0n,a1n,a2n)
(
  A = 10^(dbgain/40);
  w0 = 2*$pi*fc/srate;
  c = cos(w0);
  s = sin(w0);
  alpha = s/(2*q);
  beta = 2*sqrt(A)*alpha;

  b0n =    A*((A+1) + (A-1)*c + beta);
  b1n = -2*A*((A-1) + (A+1)*c);
  b2n =    A*((A+1) + (A-1)*c - beta);
  a0n =        (A+1) - (A-1)*c + beta;
  a1n =    2*((A-1) - (A+1)*c);
  a2n =        (A+1) - (A-1)*c - beta;

  a0 = b0n/a0n;
  a1 = b1n/a0n;
  a2 = b2n/a0n;
  b1 = a1n/a0n;
  b2 = a2n/a0n;
);

function biquad_set_peak(fc, q, dbgain)
instance(a0,a1,a2,b1,b2)
local(A,w0,c,s,alpha,b0n,b1n,b2n,a0n,a1n,a2n)
(
  fc = clamp(fc, 20, srate * 0.45);
  q = max(0.20, q);
  A = 10^(dbgain/40);
  w0 = 2*$pi*fc/srate;
  c = cos(w0);
  s = sin(w0);
  alpha = s/(2*q);

  b0n = 1 + alpha*A;
  b1n = -2*c;
  b2n = 1 - alpha*A;
  a0n = 1 + alpha/A;
  a1n = -2*c;
  a2n = 1 - alpha/A;

  a0 = b0n/a0n;
  a1 = b1n/a0n;
  a2 = b2n/a0n;
  b1 = a1n/a0n;
  b2 = a2n/a0n;
);

function biquad_tick(x)
instance(a0,a1,a2,b1,b2,x1,x2,y1,y2)
local(y)
(
  y = a0*x + a1*x1 + a2*x2 - b1*y1 - b2*y2;
  y = zap_denorm(y);
  x2 = zap_denorm(x1); x1 = zap_denorm(x);
  y2 = zap_denorm(y1); y1 = y;
  y;
);

function init_zp_meter_filters()
local(Vh,Vb,db,f0,Q,K,a0)
(
  db=3.999843853973347;
  f0=1681.974450955533;
  Q=0.7071752369554196;
  K=tan($pi*f0/srate);
  Vh=10^(db/20);
  Vb=Vh^0.4996667741545416;
  a0=1+K/Q+K*K;
  kf1a1=2*(K*K-1)/a0;
  kf1a2=(1-K/Q+K*K)/a0;
  kf1b0=(Vh+Vb*K/Q+K*K)/a0;
  kf1b1=2*(K*K-Vh)/a0;
  kf1b2=(Vh-Vb*K/Q+K*K)/a0;

  f0=38.13547087602444;
  Q=0.5003270373238773;
  K=tan($pi*f0/srate);
  a0=1+K/Q+K*K;
  kf2a1=2*(K*K-1)/a0;
  kf2a2=(1-K/Q+K*K)/a0;
  kf2b0=1;
  kf2b1=-2;
  kf2b2=1;
);

function zp_lufs_tick(x)
instance(f1p1,f1p2,f2p1,f2p2)
local(f1p0,f2p0,y)
(
  f1p0 = x - kf1a1*f1p1 - kf1a2*f1p2;
  y = kf1b0*f1p0 + kf1b1*f1p1 + kf1b2*f1p2;
  f1p2 = zap_denorm(f1p1);
  f1p1 = zap_denorm(f1p0);

  f2p0 = y - kf2a1*f2p1 - kf2a2*f2p2;
  y = kf2b0*f2p0 + kf2b1*f2p1 + kf2b2*f2p2;
  f2p2 = zap_denorm(f2p1);
  f2p1 = zap_denorm(f2p0);
  zap_denorm(y);
);

function clear_limiter_delay()
local(i)
(
  i = 0;
  loop(max_look_spl,
    bufL[i] = 0;
    bufR[i] = 0;
    bufPeak[i] = max(db2gain(lim_ceiling), 0.000000000001);
    i += 1;
  );
  writepos = 0;
  lim_gain = 1;
  lim_gain_smooth = 1;
  lim_read_spl = lim_soft_spl;
  lim_release_start = max(db2gain(lim_ceiling), 0.000000000001);
  lim_release_idx = srate;
);

function lim_attack_window(ratio)
(
  0.5 - 0.5*cos(ratio*$pi);
);

function lim_release_window(ratio)
(
  0.5 + 0.5*cos(ratio*$pi);
);

function lim_dist_sample(x)
(
  lim_dist_B*x/(lim_dist_A*abs(x) + 1);
);

function lim_scaling_for_peak(peak, limit)
(
  (limit/max(peak, 0.000000000001))^(1 - lim_sat_w);
);

function lim_distortion_for_peak(peak, limit)
(
  (1 - (limit/max(peak, 0.000000000001))^lim_sat_w)/max(limit, 0.000000000001);
);

function peak_meter_tick(pk, env)
local(v)
(
  v = max(pk, 0.000000000001);
  v > env ? v : v + peak_meter_c*(env - v);
);

// compute_dsp_params() -- definita in @init cosi' e' visibile in @slider e @sample
function compute_dsp_params()
(
  in_capture_seconds = clamp(in_capture_seconds <= 0 ? 30 : in_capture_seconds, 20, 90);
  out_capture_seconds = clamp(out_capture_seconds <= 0 ? 30 : out_capture_seconds, 20, 90);
  // Gate
  gate_sc_hpf_on = gate_hpf >= 20 ? 1 : 0;
  gate_sc_hpf_hz = min(max(gate_hpf, 20), srate*0.45);
  sc_a = exp(-2*$pi*gate_sc_hpf_hz/srate);
  gate_thr_db = gate_thresh + profile_gate;
  gate_thr_g = db2gain(gate_thr_db);
  gate_range_g = db2gain(gate_range);
  gate_hyst_g = db2gain(gate_hyst);
  gate_open_thr_g = gate_thr_g;
  gate_close_thr_g = gate_thr_g * gate_hyst_g;
  gate_curve_eff = max(0, gate_curve);
  gate_att_c = exp(-1000/(max(0.1,gate_att)*srate));
  gate_rel_c = exp(-1000/(max(1,gate_rel)*srate));
  gate_att_spl = max(1, gate_att * 0.001 * srate);
  gate_rel_spl = max(1, gate_rel * 0.001 * srate);
  gate_rel2_spl = max(gate_rel_spl, gate_rel_spl * 2.5);
  gate_hold_spl = max(0, min(0.12*srate, gate_rel_spl * 0.12));
  gate_rel_mul = db2gain(-(60/gate_rel_spl));
  gate_rel2_mul = db2gain(-(60/gate_rel2_spl));
  // 1175
  c1175_thr = c1175_thresh + profile_1175;
  c1175_ratio_eff = max(1, c1175_ratio);
  c1175_makeup_g = db2gain(c1175_makeup);
  c1175_att_c = exp(-1/(max(20,c1175_att_us)*0.000001*srate));
  c1175_rel_c = exp(-1000/(max(1,c1175_rel)*srate));
  c1175_det_c = exp(-1000/(10*srate));
  c1175_mix_w = c1175_mix*0.01;
  c1175_rel_lin_step = 26/srate;
  // LA2
  la2_thr = -40 + (100 - la2_peakred)*0.32 + profile_la2*0.3;
  la2_ratio_eff = la2_mode ? 10 : 3;
  la2_makeup_g = db2gain(la2_gain);
  la2_att_c = exp(-1000/(10*srate));
  la2_rel_c = exp(-1000/(500*srate));
  la2_det_c = exp(-1000/(40*srate));
  la2_mix_w = la2_mix*0.01;
  // Major Tom
  mt_thr = mt_thresh + profile_mt;
  mt_ratio_eff = max(1, mt_ratio);
  mt_makeup_auto = mt_automu ? ((abs(mt_thr) - (abs(mt_thr)/max(1,mt_ratio_eff-1)))*0.5) : 0;
  mt_makeup_g = db2gain(mt_makeup + mt_makeup_auto);
  mt_attack_ms = clamp(mt_attack_ms <= 0 ? 10 : mt_attack_ms, 0.2, 50);
  mt_attack_base_s = max(0.0002, mt_attack_ms * 0.001);
  mt_rms_c = mt_detect ? exp(-1000/(10*srate)) : exp(-1000/(0.25*srate));
  mt_mix_w = mt_mix*0.01;
  mt_rel_lin_step = 18/srate;
  // Shared sidechain highpass controls for compressor detectors (1175/LA2/MT).
  c1175_sc_hpf_hz = min(max(c1175_sc_hpf, 20), srate*0.45);
  la2_sc_hpf_hz = min(max(la2_sc_hpf, 20), srate*0.45);
  mt_sc_hpf_hz = min(max(mt_sc_hpf, 20), srate*0.45);
  c1175_sc_hpf_on = c1175_sc_hpf >= 20 ? 1 : 0;
  la2_sc_hpf_on = la2_sc_hpf >= 20 ? 1 : 0;
  mt_sc_hpf_on = mt_sc_hpf >= 20 ? 1 : 0;
  c1175_sc_hpf_c = exp(-2*$pi*c1175_sc_hpf_hz/srate);
  la2_sc_hpf_c = exp(-2*$pi*la2_sc_hpf_hz/srate);
  mt_sc_hpf_c = exp(-2*$pi*mt_sc_hpf_hz/srate);
  // Dense soft-peak
  dense_soft_thr_g = db2gain(-8);
  dense_soft_mix = 0.30;
  dense_soft_drive = 1.35;
  // Brown Guard tonal dynamics
  brn_in_g = db2gain(brn_in_trim);
  brn_out_g = db2gain(brn_out_trim);
  brn_wet_w = brn_mix * 0.01;
  brn_dry_w = 1 - brn_wet_w;
  brn_amount_w = brn_amount <= 100 ? brn_amount * 0.01 : 1 + (brn_amount - 100) * 0.02;
  brn_amount_cap_w = brn_amount <= 100 ? 1 : 1 + (brn_amount - 100) * 0.02;
  brn_user_amount_w = brn_points_dyn >= 0.5 ? max(0, brn_amount_w) : 1;
  brn_low_protect_w = brn_low_protect * 0.01;
  brn_f1 = min(brn_xover_lm, srate * 0.18);
  brn_f2 = min(max(brn_xover_mid * (2 ^ (brn_xmove2 * 1.15)), brn_f1 + 40), srate * 0.30);
  brn_f3 = min(max(brn_xover_high * (2 ^ (brn_xmove3 * 1.15)), brn_f2 + 80), srate * 0.42);
  brn_c1 = brn_onepole_coef(brn_f1);
  brn_c2 = brn_onepole_coef(brn_f2);
  brn_c3 = brn_onepole_coef(brn_f3);
  brn_hp_c = brn_onepole_coef(brn_hpf);
  brn_lp_c = brn_onepole_coef(brn_lpf);
  brn_attack_coef = exp(-1 / (max(1, brn_attack) * 0.001 * srate));
  brn_release_coef = exp(-1 / (max(1, brn_release) * 0.001 * srate));
  brn_env_attack = exp(-1 / (0.100 * srate));
  brn_env_release = exp(-1 / (1.200 * srate));
  brn_graph_attack_coef = exp(-brn_detect_div / (max(0.02, brn_attack * 0.001) * srate));
  brn_graph_release_coef = exp(-brn_detect_div / (max(0.05, brn_release * 0.001) * srate));
  brn_amu_env_c = exp(-1 / (1.200 * srate));
  brn_amu_rise_c = exp(-1 / (1.600 * srate));
  brn_amu_fall_c = exp(-1 / (0.450 * srate));
  brn_amu_max_db = 6;
  brn_amu_floor_db = -58;
  brn_fc1 = sqrt(20 * brn_f1);
  brn_fc2 = sqrt(brn_f1 * brn_f2);
  brn_fc3 = sqrt(brn_f2 * brn_f3);
  brn_fc4 = sqrt(brn_f3 * min(18000, srate * 0.45));
  brn_focus_q = 0.85;
  brn_focus1 = clamp(brn_fc1 * (2 ^ (brn_xmove1 * 1.60)), 20, min(20000, srate * 0.45));
  brn_focus2 = clamp(brn_fc2 * (2 ^ (brn_xmove2 * 1.35)), 20, min(20000, srate * 0.45));
  brn_focus3 = clamp(brn_fc3 * (2 ^ (brn_xmove3 * 1.35)), 20, min(20000, srate * 0.45));
  brn_focus4 = clamp(brn_fc4 * (2 ^ (brn_xmove4 * 1.60)), 20, min(20000, srate * 0.45));
  brn_user1_eff = clamp(brn_user1 * brn_user_amount_w, -6, 6);
  brn_user2_eff = clamp(brn_user2 * brn_user_amount_w, -6, 6);
  brn_user3_eff = clamp(brn_user3 * brn_user_amount_w, -6, 6);
  brn_user4_eff = clamp(brn_user4 * brn_user_amount_w, -6, 6);
  brn_pk1L.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus1, brn_focus_q, brn_user1_eff);
  brn_pk1R.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus1, brn_focus_q, brn_user1_eff);
  brn_pk2L.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus2, brn_focus_q, brn_user2_eff);
  brn_pk2R.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus2, brn_focus_q, brn_user2_eff);
  brn_pk3L.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus3, brn_focus_q, brn_user3_eff);
  brn_pk3R.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus3, brn_focus_q, brn_user3_eff);
  brn_pk4L.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus4, brn_focus_q, brn_user4_eff);
  brn_pk4R.biquad_set_peak(brn_focus4, brn_focus_q, brn_user4_eff);
  brn_t1 = -brn_slope * brn_oct_from_1k(brn_fc1);
  brn_t2 = -brn_slope * brn_oct_from_1k(brn_fc2);
  brn_t3 = -brn_slope * brn_oct_from_1k(brn_fc3);
  brn_t4 = -brn_slope * brn_oct_from_1k(brn_fc4);
  brn_hpf_slope_i = clamp(floor(brn_hpf_slope + 0.5), 0, 4);
  brn_lpf_slope_i = clamp(floor(brn_lpf_slope + 0.5), 0, 4);
  brn_cut1 = max(0, brn_cut1);
  brn_cut2 = max(0, brn_cut2);
  brn_cut3 = max(0, brn_cut3);
  brn_cut4 = max(0, brn_cut4);
  brn_boost1 = max(0, brn_boost1);
  brn_boost2 = max(0, brn_boost2);
  brn_boost3 = max(0, brn_boost3);
  brn_boost4 = max(0, brn_boost4);
  // Limiter
  lim_ceiling_g = db2gain(lim_ceiling);
  lim_soft_spl = floor(max(0, min(max_look_spl-2, ceil(lim_look*srate*0.001))));
  // Zero-latency: the voice limiter does not use lookahead or host PDC.
  pdc_delay = 0;
  pdc_bot_ch = 0;
  pdc_top_ch = 2;
  lim_rel_spl = ceil(max(1, lim_rel)*srate*0.001);
  lim_attack_c = lim_soft_spl > 0 ? exp(-1 / max(1, lim_soft_spl)) : 0;
  lim_release_c = exp(-1 / max(1, lim_rel_spl));
  lim_pre_g = db2gain(lim_pregain);
  lim_sat_w = lim_sat * 0.01;
  lim_on != last_lim_on ? (
    clear_limiter_delay();
    last_lim_on = lim_on;
  );
  last_lim_look_spl = lim_soft_spl;
  // Output + Input
  out_man_g = db2gain(out_makeup + profile_out);
  out_in_g = db2gain(out_in_gain);
  out_trim_c = exp(-1/(max(0.1,out_speed*2)*srate));
  out_trim_cap = out_trim_max;
  out_smart_capture_c = exp(-1/(max(0.2,out_speed*2)*srate));
  out_smart_capture_target_spl = floor(max(1, srate * out_capture_seconds));
  // Final output safety limiter: post Output trim, independent from the voice limiter/clipper.
  // Uses the Limiter Ceiling as final delivery ceiling when LIM is On; otherwise defaults to -1 dBFS.
  // Can be disabled via out_final_lim_on slider.
  // NOTE: +0.7dB compensation because the main limiter can overshoot by ~0.7dB
  out_final_lim_on ? (
    out_final_ceil_g = lim_on ? db2gain(lim_ceiling + 0.7) : db2gain(-1);
  ) : (
    out_final_ceil_g = 1.0; // No limiting when disabled
  );
  out_final_rel_c = exp(-1/(0.120*srate));

  // v4.1 BUS beta: post-Brown voice-bus tone trim + limiter detector tuning.
  // These are intentionally fixed for the first listening pass; GUI comes after A/B.
  bus_beta_on = 1;
  bus_tone_low_db = 0.2;
  bus_tone_body_db = -0.6;
  bus_tone_presence_db = 0.6;
  bus_tone_air_db = 0.35;
  bus_tone_air_cut_max_db = 1.8;
  bus_tone_air_target_db = -18;
  bus_tone_air_c = exp(-2*$pi*4200/srate);
  bus_tone_air_env_c = exp(-1/(0.070*srate));
  bus_tone_full_env_c = exp(-1/(0.180*srate));
  bus_tone_air_gain_c = exp(-1/(0.060*srate));
  bus_pk1L.biquad_set_peak(110, 0.70, bus_tone_low_db);
  bus_pk1R.biquad_set_peak(110, 0.70, bus_tone_low_db);
  bus_pk2L.biquad_set_peak(360, 0.80, bus_tone_body_db);
  bus_pk2R.biquad_set_peak(360, 0.80, bus_tone_body_db);
  bus_pk3L.biquad_set_peak(3100, 0.78, bus_tone_presence_db);
  bus_pk3R.biquad_set_peak(3100, 0.78, bus_tone_presence_db);
  bus_pk4L.biquad_set_peak(9200, 0.65, bus_tone_air_db);
  bus_pk4R.biquad_set_peak(9200, 0.65, bus_tone_air_db);
  lim_bus_det_hpf_hz = 120;
  lim_bus_det_hpf_c = exp(-2*$pi*lim_bus_det_hpf_hz/srate);
  lim_bus_det_floor_w = 0.35;
  lim_bus_max_gr_db = 8;
  lim_bus_min_gain = db2gain(-lim_bus_max_gr_db);
  in_trim_g = db2gain(in_trim);
  in_smart_c = exp(-1/(max(0.2,in_smart_speed)*srate));
  in_smart_meter_c = exp(-1/(0.40*srate));
  in_smart_capture_target_spl = floor(max(1, srate * in_capture_seconds));
  dbg_meter_c = exp(-1/(0.25*srate));
  smart_view_c = exp(-1/(max(1.5, in_smart_speed*1.5)*srate));
  peak_meter_c = exp(-1/(0.18*srate));
  refresh_in_smart_capture_trim();
);

max_look_spl = ceil(srate*0.08) + 8;
bufL = 0;
bufR = bufL + max_look_spl;
bufPeak = bufR + max_look_spl;
writepos = 0;
last_lim_look_spl = -1;
last_lim_on = -1;
clear_limiter_delay();

// Peak hold buffer: 20 slots for module meters (IN/GR/OUT x 6 modules + spare)
// Slots: 0=inIN 1=inOUT | 2=gIN 3=gGR 4=gOUT | 5=c1IN 6=c1GR 7=c1OUT
//        8=laIN 9=laGR 10=laOUT | 11=mtIN 12=mtGR 13=mtOUT | 14=limIN 15=limGR 16=limOUT
pkh_base = bufPeak + max_look_spl + 4;
PEAK_DECAY = 0.55;  // dB/frame decay (~16 dB/s @ 30fps -- LED resta ~1.5s)
i = 0; loop(20, pkh_base[i] = -90; i += 1;);

// ── LRA histogram — EBU R128 P95-P10 con gating relativo ────────────────
// 1024 bins × 0.1 dB/bin → range -70..+32.4 LUFS.
LRA_BINS     = 1024;
LRA_BPD      = 10;        // bins per dB (0.1 dB/bin)
METER_UPDATE = 0.100;
meter_m_win_cnt = 4;      // 400 ms
meter_s_win_cnt = 30;     // 3 s
meter_win_len = max(1, floor(METER_UPDATE * srate));
meter_i_m_win = 1 / max(1, meter_m_win_cnt * meter_win_len);
meter_i_s_win = 1 / max(1, meter_s_win_cnt * meter_win_len);
meter_rms_buf_base = pkh_base + 32;
meter_lufs_m_buf_base = meter_rms_buf_base + 8;
meter_lufs_s_buf_base = meter_lufs_m_buf_base + 8;
lufs_i_hist_cnt_base = meter_lufs_s_buf_base + 40;
lufs_i_hist_sum_base = lufs_i_hist_cnt_base + LRA_BINS;
lra_hist_base = lufs_i_hist_sum_base + LRA_BINS;
live_meter_now = lra_hist_base + LRA_BINS;
live_meter_max = live_meter_now + 8;
live_meter_hold_until = live_meter_max + 8;
memset(meter_rms_buf_base, 0, 8);
memset(meter_lufs_m_buf_base, 0, 8);
memset(meter_lufs_s_buf_base, 0, 40);
memset(lufs_i_hist_cnt_base, 0, LRA_BINS);
memset(lufs_i_hist_sum_base, 0, LRA_BINS);
memset(lra_hist_base, 0, LRA_BINS);
memset(live_meter_now, -100, 8);
memset(live_meter_max, -100, 8);
memset(live_meter_hold_until, 0, 8);
meter_win_pos = 0;
meter_win_cnt = 0;
meter_cur_buf = 0;
meter_cur_buf2 = 0;
meter_rms_block = 0;
meter_lufs_block = 0;
meter_block_active = 0;
meter_rms_m_sum = 0;
meter_lufs_m_sum = 0;
meter_lufs_s_sum = 0;
lufs_i_hist_total = 0;
lufs_i_hist_energy = 0;
lra_hist_total = 0;
lra_hist_energy = 0;
lra_recompute_cnt = 0;
ui_lra           = 0;

// runtime states
gate_env = 0; gate_gain = 1;
gate_lpL = 0; gate_lpR = 0;
gate_state = 1;
gate_phase = 2;
gate_hold_cnt = 0;
gate_key = 0;

c1175_env = 0; c1175_gr_db = 0;
la2_env = 0; la2_gr_db = 0;
mt_env = 0; mt_gr_db = 0; mt_fb_det = 0;
mt_attack_ms = 10;
mt_attack_base_s = 0.010;
c1175_sc_lpL = c1175_sc_lpR = 0;
c1175_sc_lp2L = c1175_sc_lp2R = 0;
la2_sc_lpL = la2_sc_lpR = 0;
la2_sc_lp2L = la2_sc_lp2R = 0;
mt_sc_lpL = mt_sc_lpR = 0;
mt_sc_lp2L = mt_sc_lp2R = 0;
brn_eps = 0.0000000001;
brn_detect_div = 32;
brn_detect_count = 0;
brn_g1 = brn_g2 = brn_g3 = brn_g4 = 1;
brn_tg1 = brn_tg2 = brn_tg3 = brn_tg4 = 1;
brn_gd1 = brn_gd2 = brn_gd3 = brn_gd4 = 0;
brn_e1 = brn_e2 = brn_e3 = brn_e4 = brn_eps;
brn_prime_pending = 1;
brn_just_primed = 0;
brn_actual1 = brn_actual2 = brn_actual3 = brn_actual4 = 0;
brn_corr1 = brn_corr2 = brn_corr3 = brn_corr4 = 0;
brn_user1 = brn_user2 = brn_user3 = brn_user4 = 0;
brn_xmove1 = brn_xmove2 = brn_xmove3 = brn_xmove4 = 0;
brn_band_drag = 0;
brn_band_drag_y0 = 0;
brn_band_drag_v0 = 0;
brn_band_drag_x0 = 0;
brn_band_drag_xv0 = 0;
brn_amu_on = 0;
brn_points_dyn = 0;
brn_amu_in_env = brn_amu_out_env = brn_eps;
brn_amu_gain_db = 0;
brn_amu_target_db = 0;
bus_tone_air_lpL = bus_tone_air_lpR = 0;
bus_tone_air_env = 0.000000001;
bus_tone_full_env = 0.000000001;
bus_tone_air_gain = 1;
lim_bus_det_lp1L = lim_bus_det_lp1R = 0;
lim_bus_det_lp2L = lim_bus_det_lp2R = 0;
last_brn_preset = -100;
debug_view_state = 0;
// Migration: slider49 used to be the hidden DBG flag. Old saved instances may
// load it as 0/1, which would make the new expander curve accidentally hard.
// Fix #3: non sovrascrivere valori legittimi 0-1
// La condizione originale era per migrazione da versioni vecchie, ma blocca valori validi
// gate_curve <= 1 ? gate_curve = 24;  // DISABILITATO - lascia i valori 0-1 validi
brn_max_cut = 4;
brn_max_boost = 0.8;
brn_low_protect = 90;
brn_xover_lm = 200;
brn_xover_mid = 1300;
brn_xover_high = 2600;
brn_hpf = 80;
brn_hpf_slope = 2;
brn_lpf = 17000;
brn_lpf_slope = 1;
brn_out_trim = 0;
brn_mix = 100;
brn_cut1 = 3.0;
brn_cut2 = 3.0;
brn_cut3 = 3.0;
brn_cut4 = 3.0;
brn_boost1 = 0.5;
brn_boost2 = 0.5;
brn_boost3 = 0.5;
brn_boost4 = 0.5;

lim_gain = 1;
out_trim_db = 0;
out_smart_capture_sum = 0;
out_smart_capture_count = 0;
out_smart_capture_target_spl = floor(max(1, srate * out_capture_seconds));
out_smart_capture_progress = 0;
out_smart_capture_ready = 0;
out_smart_capture_state = 0;
out_smart_capture_rms_db = -100;
out_smart_capture_trim_db = 0;
out_smart_capture_smooth_trim = 0;
out_smart_capture_confirm_time = 0;
in_smart_trim_db = 0;
in_smart_rms_env = 0.000000001;
in_smart_active = 0;
in_smart_prime_pending = 1;
in_smart_capture_sum = 0;
in_smart_capture_count = 0;
in_smart_capture_target_spl = floor(max(1, srate * in_capture_seconds));
in_smart_capture_progress = 0;
in_smart_capture_ready = 0;
in_smart_capture_state = 0;
in_smart_capture_rms_db = -100;
in_smart_capture_trim_db = 0;
in_trim_env = 0.000000001;
in_led_state = 1;
dbg_in_pre_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_in_post_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_gate_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_1175_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_la2_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_mt_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_brown_in_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_brown_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_lim_env = 0.000000001;
dbg_out_env = 0.000000001;
pk_in_pre_env = 0.000000001;
pk_in_trim_env = 0.000000001;
pk_in_post_env = 0.000000001;
pk_gate_env = 0.000000001;
pk_1175_env = 0.000000001;
pk_la2_env = 0.000000001;
pk_mt_env = 0.000000001;
pk_brown_in_env = 0.000000001;
pk_brown_env = 0.000000001;
pk_lim_env = 0.000000001;
pk_out_env = 0.000000001;
smart_view_rms_env = 0.000000001;
mt_det_active_db = -100;

rms_env = 0.000000001;
lufs_m_env = 0.000000001;
lufs_s_env = 0.000000001;
lufs_i_env = 0.000000001;
lufs_i_sum = 0;
lufs_i_count = 0;
meter_prev_play_state = 0;
meter_prime_pending = 1;
meter_just_primed = 0;
cur_lufs_m = -100;
cur_lufs_s = -100;
cur_lufs_i = -100;
rms_db = -100;
out_auto_g = 1;

lra_lo_track =  0;
lra_hi_track = -100;
ui_lra       =  0;
ui_global_lufs_m = -100;
ui_global_lufs_s = -100;
ui_input_smart_trim_db = 0;
ui_input_smart_in_db = -100;
ui_input_smart_rms_db = -100;
ui_input_smart_out_db = -100;
ui_input_smart_target_db = -18;
ui_input_smart_state = 0;
ui_input_smart_cap = 0;
ui_input_smart_progress = 0;
ui_input_smart_ready = 0;
ui_out_trim_db = 0;
ui_out_pre_auto_dbfs = -100;
ui_out_peak_dbfs = -100;
ui_out_peak_bar_dbfs = -100;
ui_out_peak_max_dbfs = -100;
out_peak_bar_dbfs = -100;
out_peak_bar_hold_spl = 0;
out_peak_hold_dbfs = -100;
out_peak_max_dbfs = -100;
out_peak_hold_spl = 0;
out_final_lim_gain = 1;
out_final_gr_db = 0;
play_declick_total = 1;
play_declick_remaining = 0;

init_zp_meter_filters();

@slider
profile_i = floor(profile + 0.5);
profile_changed = (profile_i != last_profile);
profile_gate = 0;
profile_1175 = 0;
profile_la2 = 0;
profile_mt = 0;
profile_out = 0;
dense_mode = (profile_i == 3);
ui_block_mask_i = clamp(floor(ui_block_mask + 0.5), 0, 255);
ui_block_mask != ui_block_mask_i ? (
  ui_block_mask = ui_block_mask_i;
  sliderchange(slider_mask(53));
);
// Migratione da v4.0.20: slider55 era un parametro inutilizzato con default +6.
lr_migration_done == 0 ? (
  out_target_lr > -5 ? (
    out_target_lr = clamp((out_target_lufs + out_target_rms) * 0.5, -29, -9);
    sliderchange(slider_mask(55));
  );
  lr_migration_done = 1;
);
cap_migration_done == 0 ? (
  capture_seconds >= 20 && capture_seconds <= 90 ? (
    in_capture_seconds <= 0 ? (in_capture_seconds = capture_seconds);
    out_capture_seconds <= 0 ? (out_capture_seconds = capture_seconds);
  );
  cap_migration_done = 1;
);
in_capture_seconds = clamp(in_capture_seconds <= 0 ? 30 : in_capture_seconds, 20, 90);
out_capture_seconds = clamp(out_capture_seconds <= 0 ? 30 : out_capture_seconds, 20, 90);

brn_preset_i = floor(brn_preset + 0.5);
// Project-load guard: do not apply Brown preset while REAPER is restoring sliders.
brn_initialized == 0 ? (
  brn_initialized = 1;
  last_brn_preset = brn_preset_i;
);
// Brown preset recall: dopo il load applica solo se il preset cambia davvero.
brn_initialized == 0 ? (
  // Primo avvio - forza applicazione preset
  brn_preset_i == 1 ? (
    // BAL - Balanced: controllo morbido 800-1800Hz, protezione sub e alte
    brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.0; brn_amount = 35; brn_attack = 180; brn_release = 1200;
    brn_max_cut = 3; brn_max_boost = 0.5; brn_low_protect = 90;
    // Crossover: centro a ~1300Hz, 2 ottave di span (200-2600Hz)
    brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 1300; brn_xover_high = 2600;
    // HPF morbido a 80Hz, LPF protettivo alto
    brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 18000; brn_lpf_slope = 1;
    brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
    // Cut/boost bilanciati per controllo morbido
    brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 2.0; brn_cut3 = 2.0; brn_cut4 = 0;
    brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0.3; brn_boost3 = 0.3; brn_boost4 = 0;
  );
  brn_preset_i == 2 ? (
    // SUB - Sub-cut: taglio aggressivo bassi/polsive (80-200Hz)
    brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.2; brn_amount = 50; brn_attack = 80; brn_release = 1000;
    brn_max_cut = 6; brn_max_boost = 0.3; brn_low_protect = 85;
    brn_xover_lm = 120; brn_xover_mid = 250; brn_xover_high = 800;
    brn_hpf = 100; brn_hpf_slope = 3; brn_lpf = 16000; brn_lpf_slope = 0;
    brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
    brn_cut1 = 4.0; brn_cut2 = 3.0; brn_cut3 = 0; brn_cut4 = 0;
    brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0; brn_boost3 = 0.5; brn_boost4 = 0.3;
  );
  brn_preset_i == 3 ? (
    // MID - Mid-scoop: scavo 400-1200Hz, apre alte
    brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.4; brn_amount = 45; brn_attack = 120; brn_release = 1100;
    brn_max_cut = 5; brn_max_boost = 1.0; brn_low_protect = 88;
    brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 600; brn_xover_high = 2500;
    brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 16000; brn_lpf_slope = 0;
    brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
    brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 4.5; brn_cut3 = 2.0; brn_cut4 = 0;
    brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0; brn_boost3 = 1.0; brn_boost4 = 0.8;
  );
  brn_preset_i == 4 ? (
    // AIR - De-ess: taglio sibilanti 5-8kHz, protezione alte
    brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.0; brn_amount = 55; brn_attack = 60; brn_release = 900;
    brn_max_cut = 6; brn_max_boost = 0.5; brn_low_protect = 90;
    brn_xover_lm = 300; brn_xover_mid = 1500; brn_xover_high = 5000;
    brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 12000; brn_lpf_slope = 2;
    brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
    brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 0; brn_cut3 = 2.0; brn_cut4 = 5.0;
    brn_boost1 = 0.2; brn_boost2 = 0.5; brn_boost3 = 0; brn_boost4 = 0;
  );
  brn_preset_i == 5 ? (
    // OFF - Flat: nessuna correzione
    brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.0; brn_amount = 0; brn_attack = 200; brn_release = 1400;
    brn_max_cut = 0; brn_max_boost = 0; brn_low_protect = 100;
    brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 1300; brn_xover_high = 2600;
    brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 18000; brn_lpf_slope = 1;
    brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
    brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 0; brn_cut3 = 0; brn_cut4 = 0;
    brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0; brn_boost3 = 0; brn_boost4 = 0;
  );
  brn_initialized = 1;
  last_brn_preset = brn_preset_i;
) : (
  // Già inizializzato - applica solo se cambia preset
  brn_preset_i != last_brn_preset ? (
    brn_preset_i == 0 ? (
      // Manual flat: nessuna ricetta preset, controlli visibili liberi.
      brn_in_trim = 0;
      brn_max_cut = 4; brn_max_boost = 0.8; brn_low_protect = 90;
      brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 1300; brn_xover_high = 2600;
      brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 18000; brn_lpf_slope = 1;
      brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
      brn_cut1 = 3.0; brn_cut2 = 3.0; brn_cut3 = 3.0; brn_cut4 = 3.0;
      brn_boost1 = 0.5; brn_boost2 = 0.5; brn_boost3 = 0.5; brn_boost4 = 0.5;
    );
    brn_preset_i == 1 ? (
      // BAL - Balanced: controllo morbido 800-1800Hz, protezione sub e alte
      brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.0; brn_amount = 35; brn_attack = 180; brn_release = 1200;
      brn_max_cut = 3; brn_max_boost = 0.5; brn_low_protect = 90;
      brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 1300; brn_xover_high = 2600;
      brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 18000; brn_lpf_slope = 1;
      brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
      brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 2.0; brn_cut3 = 2.0; brn_cut4 = 0;
      brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0.3; brn_boost3 = 0.3; brn_boost4 = 0;
    );
    brn_preset_i == 2 ? (
      // SUB - Sub-cut: taglio aggressivo bassi/polsive (80-200Hz)
      brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.2; brn_amount = 50; brn_attack = 80; brn_release = 1000;
      brn_max_cut = 6; brn_max_boost = 0.3; brn_low_protect = 85;
      brn_xover_lm = 120; brn_xover_mid = 250; brn_xover_high = 800;
      brn_hpf = 100; brn_hpf_slope = 3; brn_lpf = 16000; brn_lpf_slope = 0;
      brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
      brn_cut1 = 4.0; brn_cut2 = 3.0; brn_cut3 = 0; brn_cut4 = 0;
      brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0; brn_boost3 = 0.5; brn_boost4 = 0.3;
    );
    brn_preset_i == 3 ? (
      // MID - Mid-scoop: scavo 400-1200Hz, apre alte
      brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.4; brn_amount = 45; brn_attack = 120; brn_release = 1100;
      brn_max_cut = 5; brn_max_boost = 1.0; brn_low_protect = 88;
      brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 600; brn_xover_high = 2500;
      brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 16000; brn_lpf_slope = 0;
      brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
      brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 4.5; brn_cut3 = 2.0; brn_cut4 = 0;
      brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0; brn_boost3 = 1.0; brn_boost4 = 0.8;
    );
    brn_preset_i == 4 ? (
      // AIR - De-ess: taglio sibilanti 5-8kHz, protezione alte
      brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.0; brn_amount = 55; brn_attack = 60; brn_release = 900;
      brn_max_cut = 6; brn_max_boost = 0.5; brn_low_protect = 90;
      brn_xover_lm = 300; brn_xover_mid = 1500; brn_xover_high = 5000;
      brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 12000; brn_lpf_slope = 2;
      brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
      brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 0; brn_cut3 = 2.0; brn_cut4 = 5.0;
      brn_boost1 = 0.2; brn_boost2 = 0.5; brn_boost3 = 0; brn_boost4 = 0;
    );
    brn_preset_i == 5 ? (
      // OFF - Flat: nessuna correzione
      brn_in_trim = 0; brn_slope = 1.0; brn_amount = 0; brn_attack = 200; brn_release = 1400;
      brn_max_cut = 0; brn_max_boost = 0; brn_low_protect = 100;
      brn_xover_lm = 200; brn_xover_mid = 1300; brn_xover_high = 2600;
      brn_hpf = 80; brn_hpf_slope = 2; brn_lpf = 18000; brn_lpf_slope = 1;
      brn_out_trim = 0; brn_mix = 100;
      brn_cut1 = 0; brn_cut2 = 0; brn_cut3 = 0; brn_cut4 = 0;
      brn_boost1 = 0; brn_boost2 = 0; brn_boost3 = 0; brn_boost4 = 0;
    );
    last_brn_preset = brn_preset_i;
  );
);

// Profile slider sync only. Preset recall is performed by explicit GUI buttons
// (apply_profile_gfx), never automatically from @slider during project load.
profile_changed ? last_profile = profile_i;

// Ricalcola tutte le variabili DSP derivate dagli slider correnti
compute_dsp_params();

// Meter constants: aligned with ZP Loudness Meter v43 (BS.1770-style windows).
LUFS_CAL_DB = 0;

jsfx_view = (floor(gfx_view + 0.5) == 1);
apply_host_slider_visibility(jsfx_view ? 1 : 0);

@serialize
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_sum);
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_count);
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_progress);
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_ready);
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_state);
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_rms_db);
file_var(0, in_smart_capture_trim_db);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_sum);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_count);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_progress);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_ready);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_state);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_rms_db);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_trim_db);
file_var(0, out_smart_capture_smooth_trim);
file_var(0, in_capture_seconds);
file_var(0, out_capture_seconds);
// Fix #1: salva lo stato di inizializzazione Brown Guard
file_var(0, brn_initialized);
file_var(0, last_brn_preset);
// Fix #4: salva il preset Output selezionato
file_var(0, out_preset_sel);
file_var(0, brn_amu_on);
file_var(0, brn_user1);
file_var(0, brn_user2);
file_var(0, brn_user3);
file_var(0, brn_user4);
file_var(0, brn_xmove1);
file_var(0, brn_xmove2);
file_var(0, brn_xmove3);
file_var(0, brn_xmove4);
file_var(0, mt_attack_ms);
file_var(0, brn_points_dyn);
brn_amu_on = brn_amu_on >= 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
brn_points_dyn = brn_points_dyn >= 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
brn_user1 = clamp(brn_user1, -6, 6);
brn_user2 = clamp(brn_user2, -6, 6);
brn_user3 = clamp(brn_user3, -6, 6);
brn_user4 = clamp(brn_user4, -6, 6);
brn_xmove1 = clamp(brn_xmove1, -8, 8);
brn_xmove2 = clamp(brn_xmove2, -8, 8);
brn_xmove3 = clamp(brn_xmove3, -8, 8);
brn_xmove4 = clamp(brn_xmove4, -8, 8);
mt_attack_ms = clamp(mt_attack_ms <= 0 ? 10 : mt_attack_ms, 0.2, 50);
refresh_in_smart_capture_trim();
refresh_out_smart_capture_trim();
// Hidden Brown parameters are project-saved; after recall, rebuild derived DSP
// coefficients on the first audio block even if no visible slider changed.
dsp_needs_update = 1;

@block
// Unified presenza + heartbeat. Non controlla il DSP degli altri plugin.
zp_bus_refresh(ZP_BUS_ID);
// ZP Target Engine: telemetria separata per stadio, solo osservativa.
gmem[101] = ui_gate_act_db;                                  // expander GR
gmem[102] = ui_1175_act_db;                                  // 1175 GR
gmem[103] = ui_la2_act_db;                                   // LA2 GR
gmem[104] = ui_mt_act_db;                                    // Major Tom GR
gmem[105] = ui_brown_act_db;                                 // Brown activity
gmem[106] = max(ui_lim_act_db, ui_out_act_db);                // limiter/safety GR
gmem[107] = ui_global_rms_db;                                // RMS interno
gmem[108] = ui_out_peak_dbfs;                                // peak interno
zp_internal_crest = max(0, ui_out_peak_dbfs-ui_global_rms_db);
gmem[109] = max(0,min(100,100-zp_internal_crest*5));          // density estimate
gmem[110] = ui_brown_act_db + abs(bus_air_cut_db);            // brightness action estimate
gmem[111] = floor(out_auto_apply + 0.5);                      // 0 MANUAL, 1 AUTO

@sample
// Se la GUI ha cambiato uno slider, ricalcola i parametri DSP senza aspettare @slider
dsp_needs_update ? ( compute_dsp_params(); dsp_needs_update = 0; );
auto_mono_from_gfx < 0.5 ? (
  auto_mono_host_ch = num_ch;
  auto_mono_mode = num_ch < 2 ? 1 : 0;
);

meter_play_state = play_state > 0 ? 1 : 0;
meter_play_state && !meter_prev_play_state ? (
  rms_env = 0.000000001;
  lufs_m_env = 0.000000001;
  lufs_s_env = 0.000000001;
  lufs_i_env = 0.000000001;
  lufs_i_sum = 0;
  lufs_i_count = 0;
  cur_lufs_m = -100;
  cur_lufs_s = -100;
  cur_lufs_i = -100;
  rms_db = -100;
  dbg_out_env = 0.000000001;
  pk_in_pre_env = pk_in_trim_env = pk_in_post_env = 0.000000001;
  pk_gate_env = pk_1175_env = pk_la2_env = pk_mt_env = 0.000000001;
  pk_brown_in_env = pk_brown_env = pk_lim_env = pk_out_env = 0.000000001;
  smart_view_rms_env = 0.000000001;
  outL_prev = spl0;
  outR_prev = spl1;
  out_peak_bar_dbfs = -100;
  out_peak_bar_hold_spl = 0;
  out_peak_hold_dbfs = -100;
  out_peak_max_dbfs = -100;
  out_peak_hold_spl = 0;
  meter_kL.f1p1 = meter_kL.f1p2 = meter_kL.f2p1 = meter_kL.f2p2 = 0;
  meter_kR.f1p1 = meter_kR.f1p2 = meter_kR.f2p1 = meter_kR.f2p2 = 0;
  memset(meter_rms_buf_base, 0, 8);
  memset(meter_lufs_m_buf_base, 0, 8);
  memset(meter_lufs_s_buf_base, 0, 40);
  memset(lufs_i_hist_cnt_base, 0, LRA_BINS);
  memset(lufs_i_hist_sum_base, 0, LRA_BINS);
  memset(lra_hist_base, 0, LRA_BINS);
  meter_win_pos = 0;
  meter_win_cnt = 0;
  meter_cur_buf = 0;
  meter_cur_buf2 = 0;
  meter_rms_block = 0;
  meter_lufs_block = 0;
  meter_block_active = 0;
  meter_rms_m_sum = 0;
  meter_lufs_m_sum = 0;
  meter_lufs_s_sum = 0;
  lufs_i_hist_total = 0;
  lufs_i_hist_energy = 0;
  lra_hist_total = 0;
  lra_hist_energy = 0;
  lra_recompute_cnt = 0;
  ui_lra = 0;
  disp_lra = -999;
  lra_needs_reset = 0;
  meter_prime_pending = 1;
  meter_just_primed = 0;
  in_smart_prime_pending = 1;
  brn_prime_pending = 1;
  brn_just_primed = 0;
  brn_detect_count = brn_detect_div;
  clear_limiter_delay();
  out_trim_db = 0;
  out_auto_g = 1;
  play_declick_total = max(1, (lim_on ? lim_soft_spl : 0) + floor(0.005*srate));
  play_declick_remaining = play_declick_total;
);
meter_prev_play_state = meter_play_state;

inL = spl0;
inR = spl1;
pk_in_pre_env = peak_meter_tick(max(abs(inL), abs(inR)), pk_in_pre_env);
pk_in_pre_db = gain2db(pk_in_pre_env);
in_pre_sig = 0.5*(inL*inL + inR*inR);
dbg_in_pre_env = in_pre_sig + dbg_meter_c*(dbg_in_pre_env - in_pre_sig);
dbg_in_pre_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(dbg_in_pre_env,0.000000000001)));

// Primary input gain staging: manual trim.
inL *= in_trim_g;
inR *= in_trim_g;
pk_in_trim_env = peak_meter_tick(max(abs(inL), abs(inR)), pk_in_trim_env);
pk_in_trim_db = gain2db(pk_in_trim_env);
in_trim_sig = 0.5*(inL*inL + inR*inR);
in_trim_env = in_trim_sig + in_smart_meter_c*(in_trim_env - in_trim_sig);
in_trim_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(in_trim_env,0.000000000001)));

// Input Smart Capture: misura RMS full range solo dopo CAP manuale, poi applica un trim fisso.
in_smart_active = 0;
in_smart_on ? (
  in_sig = 0.5*(inL*inL + inR*inR);
  in_smart_rms_env = in_sig + in_smart_meter_c*(in_smart_rms_env - in_sig);
  in_rms_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(in_smart_rms_env,0.000000000001)));
  smart_view_rms_env = in_sig + smart_view_c*(smart_view_rms_env - in_sig);
  smart_view_rms_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(smart_view_rms_env,0.000000000001)));

  in_smart_capture_ready >= 0.5 ? (
    in_smart_capture_state = 2;
    refresh_in_smart_capture_trim();
  ) : in_smart_capture_state == 1 ? (
    meter_play_state && in_sig > 0.000000000001 ? (
      in_smart_capture_sum += in_sig;
      in_smart_capture_count += 1;
      in_smart_capture_progress = min(100, 100 * in_smart_capture_count / max(1, in_smart_capture_target_spl));
      in_smart_capture_count >= in_smart_capture_target_spl ? commit_in_smart_capture();
    ) : (
      in_smart_capture_progress = min(99.9, 100 * in_smart_capture_count / max(1, in_smart_capture_target_spl));
    );
  );

  in_smart_tgt = in_smart_capture_ready >= 0.5 ? in_smart_capture_trim_db : 0;
  in_smart_trim_db = in_smart_tgt + in_smart_c*(in_smart_trim_db - in_smart_tgt);
  in_smart_active = in_smart_capture_ready >= 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
  in_smart_g = db2gain(in_smart_trim_db);
  inL *= in_smart_g;
  inR *= in_smart_g;
	) : (
	  in_rms_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(in_smart_rms_env,0.000000000001)));
	  smart_view_rms_env = in_trim_sig + smart_view_c*(smart_view_rms_env - in_trim_sig);
	  smart_view_rms_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(smart_view_rms_env,0.000000000001)));
	  in_smart_trim_db = 0 + in_smart_c*(in_smart_trim_db - 0);
	  in_smart_prime_pending = 1;
    in_smart_capture_ready < 0.5 ? in_smart_capture_state = 0;
	);
pk_in_post_env = peak_meter_tick(max(abs(inL), abs(inR)), pk_in_post_env);
pk_in_post_db = gain2db(pk_in_post_env);
in_post_sig = 0.5*(inL*inL + inR*inR);
dbg_in_post_env = in_post_sig + dbg_meter_c*(dbg_in_post_env - in_post_sig);
dbg_in_post_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(dbg_in_post_env,0.000000000001)));

// Input target LED: LOW / OK / HOT (for manual trim guidance).
in_led_state = (pk_in_trim_db < -18) ? 0 : ((pk_in_trim_db > -6) ? 2 : 1);

// 1) Gate/Expander
s1L = inL; s1R = inR;
gate_on ? (
  gate_sc_hpf_on ? (
    gate_lpL = (1-sc_a)*s1L + sc_a*gate_lpL;
    gate_lpR = (1-sc_a)*s1R + sc_a*gate_lpR;
    keyL = s1L - gate_lpL;
    keyR = s1R - gate_lpR;
  ) : (
    keyL = s1L;
    keyR = s1R;
  );
  gate_det = max(abs(keyL), abs(keyR));
  gate_key = max(gate_det, gate_key * gate_rel2_mul);

  gate_gain_db = gain2db(max(gate_gain, 0.000000000001));
  gate_center_db = gate_thr_db + (gate_gain_db > gate_range*0.5 ? gate_hyst : 0);
  gate_key_db = gain2db(max(gate_key, 0.000000000001));
  gate_x_db = gate_key_db - gate_center_db;

  gate_curve_eff > 0.1 ? (
    gate_p = clamp((gate_x_db + gate_curve_eff*0.5) / gate_curve_eff, 0, 1);
    gate_p = gate_p*gate_p*(3 - 2*gate_p);
    gate_target_db = gate_range * (1 - gate_p);
  ) : (
    gate_target_db = gate_x_db >= 0 ? 0 : gate_range;
  );

  gate_target_g = db2gain(gate_target_db);
  gate_target_g > gate_gain ? (
    gate_gain = gate_target_g + gate_att_c*(gate_gain - gate_target_g);
  ) : (
    gate_gain = gate_target_g + gate_rel_c*(gate_gain - gate_target_g);
  );

  gate_phase = gate_gain > 0.98 ? 2 : (gate_gain <= gate_range_g*1.02 ? 0 : 3);
  gate_state = gate_gain > gate_range_g*1.02;
  gate_env = gate_key;

  s1L *= gate_gain;
  s1R *= gate_gain;
) : (
  gate_state = 1;
  gate_phase = 2;
  gate_hold_cnt = 0;
  gate_key = 0;
  gate_gain = 1;
);
pk_gate_env = peak_meter_tick(max(abs(s1L), abs(s1R)), pk_gate_env);
pk_gate_db = gain2db(pk_gate_env);
gate_sig = 0.5*(s1L*s1L + s1R*s1R);
dbg_gate_env = gate_sig + dbg_meter_c*(dbg_gate_env - gate_sig);
dbg_gate_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(dbg_gate_env,0.000000000001)));

// 2) 1175
s2L = s1L; s2R = s1R;
c1175_on ? (
  detL2 = s2L; detR2 = s2R;
  c1175_sc_hpf_on ? (
    c1175_sc_lpL = (1-c1175_sc_hpf_c)*detL2 + c1175_sc_hpf_c*c1175_sc_lpL;
    c1175_sc_lpR = (1-c1175_sc_hpf_c)*detR2 + c1175_sc_hpf_c*c1175_sc_lpR;
    detL2 -= c1175_sc_lpL;
    detR2 -= c1175_sc_lpR;
    c1175_sc_lp2L = (1-c1175_sc_hpf_c)*detL2 + c1175_sc_hpf_c*c1175_sc_lp2L;
    c1175_sc_lp2R = (1-c1175_sc_hpf_c)*detR2 + c1175_sc_hpf_c*c1175_sc_lp2R;
    detL2 -= c1175_sc_lp2L;
    detR2 -= c1175_sc_lp2R;
  );
  det2 = max(abs(detL2), abs(detR2));
  det2 = det2*det2;
  c1175_env = det2 + c1175_det_c*(c1175_env-det2);
  det2 = sqrt(max(c1175_env,0.000000000001));

  over2 = max(0, gain2db(det2) - c1175_thr);
  tgt_gr2 = -over2*(c1175_ratio_eff-1)/c1175_ratio_eff;
  tgt_gr2 < c1175_gr_db ? (
    c1175_gr_db = tgt_gr2 + c1175_att_c*(c1175_gr_db - tgt_gr2);
  ) : (
    rel_exp2 = tgt_gr2 + c1175_rel_c*(c1175_gr_db - tgt_gr2);
    dense_mode && lim_on ? (
      rel_lin2 = min(0, c1175_gr_db + c1175_rel_lin_step);
      c1175_gr_db = max(rel_exp2, rel_lin2);
    ) : (
      c1175_gr_db = rel_exp2;
    );
  );

  c1175_g = db2gain(c1175_gr_db) * c1175_makeup_g;
  wetL = s2L * c1175_g;
  wetR = s2R * c1175_g;
  s2L = wetL*c1175_mix_w + s2L*(1-c1175_mix_w);
  s2R = wetR*c1175_mix_w + s2R*(1-c1175_mix_w);
);
pk_1175_env = peak_meter_tick(max(abs(s2L), abs(s2R)), pk_1175_env);
pk_1175_db = gain2db(pk_1175_env);
comp1_sig = 0.5*(s2L*s2L + s2R*s2R);
dbg_1175_env = comp1_sig + dbg_meter_c*(dbg_1175_env - comp1_sig);
dbg_1175_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(dbg_1175_env,0.000000000001)));

// 3) LA2-style
aL = s2L; aR = s2R;
la2_on ? (
  detL3 = aL; detR3 = aR;
  la2_sc_hpf_on ? (
    la2_sc_lpL = (1-la2_sc_hpf_c)*detL3 + la2_sc_hpf_c*la2_sc_lpL;
    la2_sc_lpR = (1-la2_sc_hpf_c)*detR3 + la2_sc_hpf_c*la2_sc_lpR;
    detL3 -= la2_sc_lpL;
    detR3 -= la2_sc_lpR;
    la2_sc_lp2L = (1-la2_sc_hpf_c)*detL3 + la2_sc_hpf_c*la2_sc_lp2L;
    la2_sc_lp2R = (1-la2_sc_hpf_c)*detR3 + la2_sc_hpf_c*la2_sc_lp2R;
    detL3 -= la2_sc_lp2L;
    detR3 -= la2_sc_lp2R;
  );
  det3 = 0.5*(detL3*detL3 + detR3*detR3);
  la2_env = det3 + la2_det_c*(la2_env-det3);
  det3 = sqrt(max(la2_env,0.000000000001));

  over3 = max(0, gain2db(det3) - la2_thr);
  tgt_gr3 = -over3*(la2_ratio_eff-1)/la2_ratio_eff;
  ccoef3 = tgt_gr3 < la2_gr_db ? la2_att_c : la2_rel_c;
  la2_gr_db = tgt_gr3 + ccoef3*(la2_gr_db-tgt_gr3);

  la2_g = db2gain(la2_gr_db)*la2_makeup_g;
  wetL = aL * la2_g;
  wetR = aR * la2_g;
  aL = wetL*la2_mix_w + aL*(1-la2_mix_w);
  aR = wetR*la2_mix_w + aR*(1-la2_mix_w);
);
pk_la2_env = peak_meter_tick(max(abs(aL), abs(aR)), pk_la2_env);
pk_la2_db = gain2db(pk_la2_env);
la2_sig = 0.5*(aL*aL + aR*aR);
dbg_la2_env = la2_sig + dbg_meter_c*(dbg_la2_env - la2_sig);
dbg_la2_db = gain2db(sqrt(max(dbg_la2_env,0.000000000001)));

// 4) MajorTom-style
bL = aL; bR = aR;
mt_on ? (
  srcL = mt_source ? (bL*0.7 + mt_fb_det*0.3) : bL;
  srcR = mt_source ? (bR*0.7 + mt_fb_det*0.3) : bR;
  mt_sc_hpf_on ? (
    mt_sc_lpL = (1-mt_sc_hpf_c)*srcL + mt_sc_hpf_c*mt_sc_lpL;
    mt_sc_lpR = (1-mt_sc_hpf_c)*srcR + mt_sc_hpf_c*mt_sc_lpR;
    srcL -= mt_sc_lpL;
    srcR -= mt_sc_lpR;
    mt_sc_lp2L = (1-mt_sc_hpf_c)*srcL + mt_sc_hpf_c*mt_sc_lp2L;
    mt_sc_lp2R = (1-mt_sc_hpf_c)*srcR + mt_sc_hpf_c*mt_sc_lp2R;
    srcL -= mt_sc_lp2L;
    srcR -= mt_sc_lp2R;
  );
  pk4 = max(abs(srcL),abs(srcR));
  det4 = mt_detect ? (0.5*(srcL*srcL + srcR*srcR)) : (pk4*pk4);
  mt_env = det4 + mt_rms_c*(mt_env - det4);
  det4 = sqrt(max(mt_env,0.000000000001));
  mt_det_active_db = gain2db(det4);

  over4 = max(0, gain2db(det4) - mt_thr);
  dyn_att = exp(-1/(max(0.0002, mt_attack_base_s/(1+over4))*srate));
  dyn_rel = exp(-1/(max(0.03, over4/125 + 0.05)*srate));

  ratio4 = mt_knee ? (1 + (mt_ratio_eff-1)*min(over4,6)/6) : mt_ratio_eff;
  tgt_gr4 = -over4*(ratio4-1)/ratio4;
  tgt_gr4 < mt_gr_db ? (
    mt_gr_db = tgt_gr4 + dyn_att*(mt_gr_db - tgt_gr4);
  ) : (
    rel_exp4 = tgt_gr4 + dyn_rel*(mt_gr_db - tgt_gr4);
    dense_mode && lim_on ? (
      rel_lin4 = min(0, mt_gr_db + mt_rel_lin_step);
      mt_gr_db = max(rel_exp4, rel_lin4);
